# Claude Certified Architect Foundations (CCAR-F): Quick Reference

> This sheet isn't everything on the exam — it's the things you can't work out
> on the day. Much of the CCAR-F rewards reasoning: given solid architectural
> instincts, you can derive your way to the right answer on tool design,
> orchestration, and error handling. But some answers are pure convention: which
> file lives where, which flag does what, what each `stop_reason` means. Those
> you either know or you don't, and the exam is closed-book. This is my
> collection of the ones worth committing to memory.

