## Claude API: `stop_reason`

Every response carries a `stop_reason` telling you why model generation halted.
For agent loops, the `tool_use` vs `end_turn` distinction is what drives the
loop.

- **`end_turn`** — Claude has finished; surface the reply to the user.
- **`tool_use`** — Claude wants a tool run; execute it and feed the result back.
- **`max_tokens`** — the output cap was hit; the reply is truncated, so consider
  raising the limit.
- **`stop_sequence`** — a configured stop string was encountered.

