## CLI for CI/CD

- **`claude -p` (`--print`)** — non-interactive run: prompt in, result to
  stdout, exit. The only way to drive Claude in a pipeline such as CI/CD.
- **`--output-format json`** — emit JSON; **`--json-schema`** — validate that
  output against a schema.
- **Do code reviews with a fresh instance:** the session that wrote the code is
  a weaker reviewer of it, being anchored to its own reasoning. Spin up an
  independent one.
- **To avoid repeat comments on re-review:** feed in the prior review and
  instruct Claude to flag only new or still-open issues.

---

## Sessions — Resume and Fork

- **`claude -r` / `--resume <name>`** — picks a named session back up; be sure
  to watch for stale tool results if files have moved on since.
- **`fork_session`** — branches the current context into independent lines that
  share everything up to the split, then diverge. Good for trialling two
  different approaches side by side.

